<p style="text-align: center;"><strong>Posting deadline:</strong> April 5th at 11:59 PM</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><strong>Voting deadline:</strong> April 26th at 11:59 PM <strong>OR</strong> exactly 3 weeks after the last person posts.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-1')">1</a></sup></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">As always, you can still post during the voting period, but you'll have less time to accumulate votes.</p>
<p style="text-align: center;">What about the people who already posted their Round 4 entries, you ask? Well, only votes from the first three weeks after the article was posted will be counted. Thanks, scpper!</p>
